{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "JnygO",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Descubrir",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "UiqU2",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Descubrir",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mAIcs",
          "name": "Lede",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The one surface that reads the world instead of the instance. It answers \"what moved without me?\" — the antidote to a portfolio bubble. Decided in D31.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "c4QfB",
          "name": "Entry point",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Entry point",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "q5Z0ie",
          "name": "EntryBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Route /discover · label \"Descubrir\" · fifth shell destination, inserted at position 3 so Panorama / Activos / Reglas keep their place and only Ajustes shifts. Not named \"Mercado\": /market/:symbol stays the asset detail (S4 Camila).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "o6I8mv",
          "name": "Kit",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Kit",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "UNeQ2",
          "name": "KitBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source 0.6.0. The fifth destination is CANONICAL in the kit now (BottomNav + SidebarNav, ui-kit 0.6.0), not the local override this file carried while it was drafted. All four shell-drawing flows re-vendored on 2026-08-25; auth and onboarding draw no shell and needed no re-sync. AppShellDesktop took the change for free — it instances SidebarNav by ref instead of copying it.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "mO4xE",
          "name": "The four blocks",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The four blocks",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V7c25N",
          "name": "BlocksBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Olas — fixed 17-basket ranked by the move SINCE THE LAST VISIT (capped at 90 days), not a fixed 30-day window. A weekly visitor is not served by a month-long ruler, and `discover:last_seen` is already stored for the kill criterion, so the window costs nothing (C5 Renata, cap by S2 Adriana).\nCalendario — next Banxico + Fed announcements, from a YAML in the repo. The ONLY block that needs no credential (C8 Bram).\nReportan pronto — upcoming earnings for the baskets' bellwethers.\nTitulares — five headlines FILTERED to the baskets' symbols. Unfiltered it is a news river, stale at a weekly cadence; anchored to the baskets it stops being \"news\" and becomes why SMH moved (C1 Lucía).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V1m39H",
          "name": "The basket (17)",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The basket (17)",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "j8QHS",
          "name": "BasketBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "SPY as the baseline · EWW VGK EWJ INDA MCHI (geography) · XLK SMH XLE XLF XLV (US sectors) · ARKK URA COPX BOTZ (themes) · GLD TLT (thermometers).\nIt lives in a YAML beside the calendar's, not a Ruby constant: hardcoded in Ruby, a self-hoster edits code to change their own basket and loses it on the next pull (C8 Bram).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "OCVIa",
          "name": "Disposability contract",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Disposability contract",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "D0w8p",
          "name": "ContractBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Zero tables, zero migrations, zero rows — all of it in Rails.cache.\nOne job, WarmDiscoverJob every 4h, writing with a 24h TTL so a failed run serves stale data instead of an empty screen.\nZero events. Never WRITES to Asset — the only bridge in is an explicit \"Agregar a Rastreados\". Reading is not writing: the screen reads open positions to mark exposure per basket, which clause 5 permits and D31 now states outright.\nOne folder, so deleting it is that folder plus a route, a nav entry, a job and a recurring.yml line.\nKill criterion: eight weeks after merge, deleted unless opened in 4 of those 8.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Xrn39",
          "name": "States",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "States",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JwVD2",
          "name": "StatesBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Default (this row) and Sin datos — no credential, or the job has never run. \"Dato viejo\" is NOT an artboard: it swaps the header subtitle to \"actualizado hace 6 h\" and nothing else moves.\nDesktop: only the Default artboard is drawn (D4). Two columns — Olas at native row width on the left, the other three stacked right; the columns are never widened, the screen buys more rows. Sin datos reflows into the same shell with the notice and the Calendario alone, so it earns no artboard.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cuReL",
          "name": "Findings",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Findings",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "uYZN1",
          "name": "FindingsBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "N1 — WaveRow derives from the kit's AssetRow minus its confluence block. \"oportunidad\" is advice and ADR-0001 forbids it on a screen about symbols the user does not hold.\nN2 — \"vs SPY\" separates a real wave from a rising tide. Groundable, SPY is in the basket.\nN3 — the sparkline needs a ~30-point daily series per basket symbol. One batched bars call, not 17.\nN4 — \"referentes de las canastas\" needs a bellwether map (SMH -> NVDA, XLE -> XOM, URA -> CCJ). Same YAML as the basket.\nN5 — the calendar dates drawn here are placeholders. The real ones come from the repo YAML.\nN6 — the Activos brief this file was seeded from was deleted before it was read, so this brief follows design/README's spec rather than that file's exact shape.\nN7 — the exposure chip is the panel's real finding (C6 Esther): without it the screen answers \"what moved?\", which is trivia, instead of \"am I missing something?\", which is the reason the tab exists. The chips are drawn against the real AssetCatalog — NVDA and OKE are seeded, so SMH and XLE read as covered.\nN8 — the chip is styled NEUTRALLY in both states, on purpose. Colouring \"sin exposición\" would read as \"act here\", which is the advice ADR-0001 forbids. The information is in the words, not in the fill.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
